From: ARLinux contributors
Subject: [PATCH] dxvk: explicitly construct the null fragment pipeline key

Use the same key construction as other pipeline library insertions. This
also avoids libc++ 23's invalid tuple_element<0, tuple<>> instantiation
when emplacing a default-constructed key with an empty tuple.

diff --git a/src/dxvk/dxvk_pipemanager.cpp b/src/dxvk/dxvk_pipemanager.cpp
--- a/src/dxvk/dxvk_pipemanager.cpp
+++ b/src/dxvk/dxvk_pipemanager.cpp
@@ -394,7 +394,7 @@
 
     auto iter = m_shaderLibraries.emplace(
       std::piecewise_construct,
-      std::tuple(),
+      std::tuple(key),
       std::tuple(m_device, this, key));
     return &iter.first->second;
   }
